<section class="card mt-3" aria-label="Hidden FX catalog routes">
    <div class="card-header py-1 fw-bold text-info">Hidden FX catalog and carrier routes</div>
    <div class="card-body py-2">
        <p class="small mb-2">
            This catalog exposes the native routes found during the FX inventory pass.
            A <strong>preload</strong> result means the game can decode the resource; it does
            not make a particle model a portable item. Promotion to an item requires native
            preload, placement, visible play, map save/reopen and a cold restart.
        </p>
        <div class="row g-2 align-items-end mb-2" aria-label="Native FX carrier selection">
            <div class="col-md-7">
                <label class="form-label small mb-1" for="fxCarrierPreset">FX carrier preset</label>
                <select id="fxCarrierPreset" class="form-select form-select-sm" @bind="selectedCarrierName">
                    @foreach (var route in ProvenCarrierRoutes)
                    {
                        <option value="@route.Name">@route.Name</option>
                    }
                </select>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-5 small text-muted" role="status">
                <strong class="text-info">@SelectedCarrier.Name</strong><br />
                @SelectedCarrier.Scope
                <span class="badge @SelectedCarrier.StatusBadge ms-1">@SelectedCarrier.Status</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="small text-muted mb-2">
            The preset list is intentionally limited to carriers with native evidence. Choosing a preset records the
            intended carrier route for the Studio session; it does not rewrite an opaque particle graph. Particle-model
            replacement becomes an export option only after that model passes the same native preload, visible placement,
            save/reopen and cold-start checks.
        </p>
        <div class="row g-2 align-items-end mb-2" aria-label="Particle model candidate selection">
            <div class="col-md-7">
                <label class="form-label small mb-1" for="fxParticleCandidate">Particle model to emit</label>
                <select id="fxParticleCandidate" class="form-select form-select-sm" @bind="selectedParticleCandidate">
                    @foreach (var route in ParticleCandidateRoutes)
                    {
                        <option value="@route.Name">@route.Name</option>
                    }
                </select>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-5 small text-muted" role="status">
                <strong class="text-info">@SelectedParticleCandidate.Name</strong><br />
                @SelectedParticleCandidate.Scope
                <span class="badge @SelectedParticleCandidate.StatusBadge ms-1">@SelectedParticleCandidate.Status</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="row g-2 align-items-end mb-2" aria-label="Complete FX particle inventory">
            <div class="col-md-7">
                <label class="form-label small mb-1" for="fxParticleAudit">Exact particle model (83-row native audit)</label>
                <select id="fxParticleAudit" class="form-select form-select-sm" @bind="selectedParticleAudit">
                    @foreach (var particle in ParticleAuditRoutes)
                    {
                        <option value="@particle.Name">@particle.Name — @particle.Status</option>
                    }
                </select>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-5 small text-muted" role="status">
                <strong class="text-info">@SelectedParticleAudit.Name</strong><br />
                @SelectedParticleAudit.Context · @SelectedParticleAudit.Evidence
                <span class="badge @SelectedParticleAudit.StatusBadge ms-1">@SelectedParticleAudit.Status</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p class="small text-muted mb-2">
            This exact-model selector is an audit and route picker. It does not replace the complete native carrier graph;
            only rows marked <strong>item-carrier-proven</strong> are eligible for the current preserve-and-origin-edit export.
        </p>
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm align-middle mb-2">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Route / candidate</th>
                        <th scope="col">Native evidence</th>
                        <th scope="col">Studio use</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (var route in Routes)
                    {
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="row" class="small">
                                <span class="badge @route.TierBadge me-1">@route.Tier</span>
                                @route.Name
                            </th>
                            <td class="small">@route.Evidence</td>
                            <td class="small"><span class="badge @route.StatusBadge">@route.Status</span><span class="ms-1">@route.Scope</span></td>
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <details class="small">
            <summary class="text-info">What the hidden inventory contains</summary>
            <p class="mt-2 mb-1">The complete 83-model inventory contains leaves, fog, vehicle smoke/fire/boost, sparkles, light trails, water spray/splash, bubbles, wakes and ShootMania effects. The read-only native pass recorded 54 preloads, 7 null-node failures and 22 parser skips. Context-bound assets or models without an item wrapper remain discovery candidates.</p>
            <p class="mb-0">The safe authoring route is an existing embedded carrier. Studio currently edits its validated emitter origin and preserves the complete opaque graph; it does not invent graph nodes or dependencies.</p>
        </details>
    </div>
</section>

